[555.18959, "o", "\u001b[0m$ \u001b[0mcd /app && python - <<'EOF'\r\nexec(open('/tmp/tune.py').read().split(\"if __name__\")[0])\r\nbase=open('model_ref.xml').read()\r\ndef mk(o): return base.replace('<compiler autolimits=\"true\"/>', o+'<compiler autolimits=\"true\"/>')\r\nfor it in [100,150,200]:\r\n    o=f'<option solver=\"PGS\" iterations=\"{it}\" tolerance=\"1e-10\"/>'\r\n    open('/tmp/cand.xml','w').write(mk(o))\r\n    m=mujoco.MjModel.from_xml_path('/tmp/cand.xml')\r\n    diffs=[np.max(np.abs(sim(m,s)-sim(mref,s))) for s in range(60)]\r\n    ts=timed(m,10)\r\n    print(f'it={it} maxdiff={max(diffs):.3e} mean={np.mean(diffs):.3e} pctg={ts.mean()/timed(mref,10).mean():.3f}')\r\nEOF\r\nit=100 maxdiff=3.899e-07 mean=7.150e-08 pctg=0.497\r\nit=150 maxdiff=3.899e-07 mean=7.150e-08 pctg=0.508\r\nit=200 maxdiff=3.899e-07 mean=7.150e-08 pctg=0.498\r\n"]
[556.177153, "o", "> build · deepseek-v4.1-flash\r\n"]
[621.139645, "o", "\u001b[0m$ \u001b[0mcd /app && python - <<'EOF'\r\nimport mujoco, numpy as np\r\nfrom eval import simulate_model\r\nm=mujoco.MjModel.from_xml_path('model.xml')\r\nr=mujoco.MjModel.from_xml_path('model_ref.xml')\r\nworst=0; mind=1\r\nfor s in range(150):\r\n    a=simulate_model(m,s); b=simulate_model(r,s)\r\n    d=np.max(np.abs(a-b)); worst=max(worst,d)\r\nprint('max abs state diff over 150 seeds:', worst)\r\nprint('nq,nv,nbody:',m.nq,m.nv,m.nbody,'| timestep',m.opt.timestep,'| solver',m.opt.solver)\r\nEOF\r\nmax abs state diff over 150 seeds: 3.899271519315628e-07\r\nnq,nv,nbody: 157 118 42 | timestep 0.002 | solver 0\r\n"]
[622.246654, "o", "> build · deepseek-v4.1-flash\r\n"]
[623.598154, "o", "Done. `/app/model.xml` is created and passing.\r\n\r\n## What changed\r\n\r\nOnly the constraint solver options were tuned — no physical properties, geometry, masses, damping, timestep, or the cable plugin config were touched:\r\n\r\n```xml\r\n<option solver=\"PGS\" iterations=\"200\" tolerance=\"1e-10\"/>\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe original used the default Newton solver, whose sparse factorization dominated per-step cost (≈161 µs of a ≈275 µs step). This model has no contacts and only a single equality constraint, so PGS converges very quickly and cheaply.\r\n\r\n## Results\r\n\r\n- `eval.py` output:\r\n  - Final state difference: `0.0000`\r\n  - Avg sim time: `~0.140 s` vs ref `~0.281 s`\r\n  - Speedup: `~2.0x`\r\n  - **Time pctg: 0.50** (target ≤ 0.60)\r\n- Robustness check over 150 random initial-condition seeds: max absolute state difference `3.9e-07`, well inside `atol=1e-5`, with no NaN/Inf.\r\n\r\n`/app/model_ref.xml` was left unchanged.\r\n"]
